JDK (Java Development Kit) — Tools used to develop Java applications.
JRE (Java Runtime Environment) — Environment used to run Java applications.
JVM (Java Virtual Machine) — Executes Java bytecode.
Maven — Java build and dependency management tool.
Gradle — Build automation tool.
JAR (Java Archive) — Package format for Java applications.
WAR (Web Application Archive) — Package format for Java web applications.
Jenkins — Automation server used to create CI/CD pipelines.
Pipeline — Automated sequence of software delivery steps.
Artifact — Output created by a build process.
CDN (Content Delivery Network) — Network used to deliver content closer to users.
