IaC (Infrastructure as Code) — Creating and managing infrastructure using code.
HCL (HashiCorp Configuration Language) — Language used to write Terraform configuration.
TF (Terraform) — Infrastructure as Code tool used to create cloud resources.
State File — File that stores Terraform infrastructure information.
Provider — Plugin used by Terraform to communicate with a platform.
Module — Reusable collection of Terraform configuration.
Backend — Location where Terraform state is stored.
DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) — Principle of avoiding duplicate code.
📊 MONITORING & OBSERVABILITY TERMS
APM (Application Performance Monitoring) — Monitors application performance.
NMS (Network Management System) — Monitors and manages networks.
SIEM (Security Information and Event Management) — Collects and analyzes security logs.
ELK (Elasticsearch, Logstash, Kibana) — Stack used for centralized logging and log analysis.
EFK (Elasticsearch, Fluentd, Kibana) — Logging stack that uses Fluentd.
SLI (Service Level Indicator) — Metric that measures service performance.
SLO (Service Level Objective) — Target value for service performance.
SLA (Service Level Agreement) — Formal agreement about service performance.
MTTR (Mean Time to Repair/Recovery) — Average time required to restore a failed system.
MTBF (Mean Time Between Failures) — Average operating time between system failures.
KPI (Key Performance Indicator) — Metric used to measure performance.
CPU (Central Processing Unit) Utilization — Percentage of processor capacity being used.
OOM (Out of Memory) — Situation where a system has insufficient memory.
